## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to model partitioning with a simple per-block objective and reconstruct optimal cuts. It reveals DP formulation, range queries, and backtracking.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP across two dimensions (prefix and blocks)
- Range maximum precomputation or on-the-fly tracking
- Backpointers for path reconstruction
- Time/space trade-offs and potential optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function minPartitionCostMax(A, m){
  const n = A.length;
  // precompute max for all ranges
  const rangeMax = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    let cur = 0;
    for(let j=i;j<n;j++){
      cur = Math.max(cur, A[j]);
      rangeMax[i][j] = cur;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(m+1).fill(Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(m+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let j=1;j<=Math.min(i,m);j++){
      for(let t=j-1; t<=i-1; t++){
        const val = dp[t][j-1] + rangeMax[t][i-1];
        if(val < dp[i][j]){
          dp[i][j] = val;
          par[i][j] = t;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct
  const cuts = [];
  let i = n, j = m;
  while(j>0){
    const t = par[i][j];
    cuts.push(i);
    i = t;
    j--;
  }
  cuts.reverse();
  return {cost: dp[n][m], partitions: cuts};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you optimize to O(n m) time using monotonic queues?  
- How would you adapt if each chapter cost were max(A[t..i-1]) + c*(i-t)?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests precise DP construction for selecting k disjoint subarrays with per-subarray penalty, a common optimization variant.

## Key Concepts
- Disjoint subarray DP with two states
- Transition derivation for starting/continuing a subarray
- Space/time trade-offs and reconstruction

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSumKSubarrays(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const end = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const best = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  best[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) {
    for (let t=0; t<=k; t++) {
      end[i][t] = Math.max(end[i-1][t] + A[i-1], t>0 ? best[i-1][t-1] + A[i-1] : NEG);
      best[i][t] = Math.max(best[i-1][t], end[i][t] - c);
    }
  }
  return {value: best[n][k], subs: null};
}
```

